# Paths that need a review from the owning team before they can merge.
#
# CODEOWNERS syntax, last match wins, but a different rule. `.github/CODEOWNERS`
# is GitHub's own gate and counts nothing but an approval from the listed team,
# which breaks two things we rely on: a `stamphog[bot]` approval never satisfies
# it, and it cannot tell an owning team's own PR from another team's. This file is
# checked by .github/scripts/require-owner-review.js instead, which:
#   - passes when the author is on the owning team, so stamphog still merges our own work,
#   - passes on an approval from any member of that team,
#   - ignores generated files, lockfiles and snapshots.
#
# Adding a path here makes other teams wait for you, so read the note at the top
# of CODEOWNERS first. The same bar applies. An owner-less line resets a subtree.

# Workflows owns CDP, Workflows and Messaging end to end: the product trees and the
# plugin-server workers that run them. Other teams edit these trees as a side effect
# of shipping their own product, usually by carving out an exception so their own rows
# behave differently. A mistake there is silent: nothing errors, their tests still
# pass, and existing customer configurations stop being listed, or stop being
# delivered. #66355 did that, and it took #83993, #86202 and #86614 to unwind.
products/cdp/** @PostHog/team-workflows
products/workflows/** @PostHog/team-workflows
products/messaging/** @PostHog/team-workflows
nodejs/src/cdp/** @PostHog/team-workflows
